### 2. Standard or Itemize?
You should likely take the **Standard Deduction**. 
For 2023, the standard deduction for a single filer is **$13,850**. To itemize, your eligible personal deductions (like your $800 charitable donation to Doctors Without Borders and up to $10,000 in state/local taxes) would need to exceed $13,850. Since they likely do not, taking the standard deduction will save you more money. *(Note: Your business expenses and home office are deducted separately on Schedule C, so you still get those benefits even if you take the standard deduction!)*

### 3. How to Handle the Home Office?
